2026-06-08T08:00:24Z	Matt Reider	delivered	termkrush/Zoomable-clip-editor-windowed-bar-zoom-follow-the-active-handle.md	Real zoom in the clip editor. The bar shows a WINDOW of the clip at a zoom level — +/- cycle whole→10s→1s→100ms→10ms; arrows nudge the active handle ~one column of the window, so the more you zoom the finer the step (sample-close at 10ms). The window FOLLOWS the active handle: Tab to the OUT handle and the view scrolls to the tail (the arrow-shaped things are the in ◀ / out ▸ handles). A full-clip minimap line shows where the window + handles sit; readout shows in/out in ms (3dp). Space audition, Enter snip, Esc close. Test (exit 0): a 60s clip — whole-zoom Right jumps >10k frames; +×4 → 10ms window → Right moves 7 frames. clippy + 8 suites exit 0. DELIVERED — open a long clip, +/- to zoom, Tab to flip to the end, trim to the ms.
